# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit .env (.gitignore line 5).
#
# Fill the values, leave the names alone. Every consumer reads these from the
# environment rather than from an argument: a credential passed on a command
# line lands in shell history and in the process list of everyone on the box.

# ── environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# research  historical Parquet only, and CANNOT hold broker credentials
# paper     the paper engine, real feed, no real orders
# live      real money, and needs a second arming signal on top of this
#
# Keep this on `research` until the keys below are actually filled. The env
# module refuses to load credentials in research by construction rather than
# by convention, so a half-filled file fails loudly instead of half-working.
MARKETSAGE_ENV=research


# ── Angel One SmartAPI ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# https://smartapi.angelbroking.com → My Apps → Create App. Free.
#
# ANGEL_API_KEY      the app's API key from the SmartAPI dashboard
# ANGEL_CLIENT_CODE  your Angel One login ID (looks like A123456)
# ANGEL_PIN          the 4-digit PIN you log in with
# ANGEL_TOTP_SECRET  the base32 secret behind the authenticator QR code, not
#                    the six digits it shows. Angel reveals it once when TOTP
#                    is enabled; if you only kept the QR, re-enable it.
#
# The TOTP secret is the one people get wrong, and it fails in the worst
# possible way: a six-digit code logs in once and then fails every morning
# after, which reads as a broken adapter rather than as a wrong field.
#
# Check them with `python tasks.py angel-check` the evening before, not at
# 09:14. Add --connect to actually log in.
# ANGEL_API_KEY=
# ANGEL_CLIENT_CODE=
# ANGEL_PIN=
# ANGEL_TOTP_SECRET=


# ── Upstox (recommended: free, and no daily login) ───────────────────────
# An **Analytics Token** from the Upstox developer console: one year of
# validity, read-only. Read-only is the point - the recorder physically
# cannot place an order, which is a stronger guarantee than MARKETSAGE_ENV
# because it is enforced at the venue rather than by this repository.
#
# A daily OAuth access token also works in the same field, but it expires the
# next trading day, so an unattended recorder fails on a morning nobody is
# watching.
# UPSTOX_ACCESS_TOKEN=


# ── Kite (Zerodha), if ever used instead ─────────────────────────────────
# Redirect URL for the developer console: http://127.0.0.1:5000/callback
# KITE_API_KEY=
# KITE_API_SECRET=


# ── Hugging Face ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A **Write** token from https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens. A Read token
# authenticates fine and then fails when the Space is created, which reads as
# a permissions bug rather than as a wrong token type.
# HF_TOKEN=


# ── live arming ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The second of two signals. The other is a .live-armed file at the repo
# root. Both are required, and the friction is deliberate.
# MARKETSAGE_LIVE_ARMED=1
